# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD formats the KRaft storage, starts the Kafka broker in the
# BACKGROUND with the vulnerable PLAINTEXT config, waits for 9092 to bind, then
# execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the broker is ALREADY RUNNING with an unauthenticated PLAINTEXT client
#     listener when the agent starts (the vulnerability is live);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, not the broker, so stopping/restarting the
#     broker cannot kill the container.
#
# The remediation rewrites /opt/kafka/config/server.properties to require
# SASL_PLAINTEXT/PLAIN on the client listener and RESTARTS the broker. There IS a
# "forgot to restart" case: editing the config without restarting leaves the live
# broker still serving PLAINTEXT, which the behavioural check detects.
